event: delegated_tool_call
data: {"agent":"coordinator","agent_tab":"coordinator","event":{"tool_input":{"content":"# Self-Evolution Daily Monitor — Day 01\n## Task Family: `duplicate_merge_probe`\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-25  \n**Run scope:** Bounded filesystem evidence only. Generic, application-neutral.  \n**Method:** Slug similarity, trigger/description overlap, procedure overlap, telemetry evidence cross-reference.  \n**No skills were mutated, created, or deleted in this report.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. Inventory Summary\n\nThe `available_skills/` directory contains **26 skill directories** as of this scan. They break into the following clusters for duplicate analysis:\n\n| Cluster | Count | Directories |\n|---------|-------|-------------|\n| **Figma design** | 2 | `figma`, `figma_mcp` |\n| **GitNexus** | 7 | `gitnexus_cli`, `gitnexus_debugging`, `gitnexus_exploring`, `gitnexus_guide`, `gitnexus_impact_analysis`, `gitnexus_pr_review`, `gitnexus_refactoring` |\n| **Materialization pipeline** | 3 | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry`, `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path`, `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` |\n| **Telemetry** | 1 | `telemetry_optimization` |\n| **Experimental auto-generated** | 5 | `skill-exp-052e6a93-9680-4a98-bc7a-441abfc18c46-1779612141421504000`, `skill-exp-2b07b1df-173c-47ad-aa62-8a076cd6c26c-1779618706105440000`, `skill-exp-4d613241-8b59-45ad-8daa-d5cb5dc1fb3e-1779613286395772000`, `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_6797_40d8_ba1a_d53409bb4536_1779616302740038000`, `skill_exp_1590b4d7_0aa7_4d87_ad40_14e222b2394b_1779614687697856000` |\n| **Financial market** | 2 | `stock_analysis`, `crypto_market` |\n| **Development tools** | 5 | `chronicle`, `golang`, `openspec`, `playwright_mcp`, `shadcn_ui` |\n| **Data/utility** | 1 | `weather` |\n\nAdditionally, the `skills/` mirror directory (promotion source) contains **4 overlapping entries** — these are the same materialization + telemetry skills in a different lifecycle state, not duplicates.\n\n**Skills with `_meta.json` convention compliance:** 4 of 26 (15%) — `crypto_market`, `playwright_mcp`, `stock_analysis`, `weather`. The remaining 22 directories lack `_meta.json`, meaning they cannot participate in registry-based lifecycle management until remediated.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Cluster Analysis: Slug Similarity\n\n### 2.1 — Matched pairs by slug stem\n\n| Pair | Stem(s) | Slug A | Slug B | Similarity |\n|------|---------|--------|--------|------------|\n| **P1** | `figma` | `figma` | `figma-mcp` | **HIGH** — identical stem `figma`; suffix `-mcp` denotes tool layer only |\n| **P2** | `materialization-*` | `materialization-activation-telemetry-registry` | `materialization-proposal-linked-skill-package-registry-load-path` | **HIGH** — both start `materialization-`; share 4/5 keyword blocks |\n| **P3** | `materialization-*` | `materialization-activation-telemetry-registry` | `materialization-skill-package-registry-load-path-usage-telemetry` | **HIGH** — share 5/5 keyword blocks: `materialization`, `registry`, `telemetry`, `load-path` |\n| **P4** | `materialization-*` | `materialization-proposal-linked-skill-package-registry-load-path` | `materialization-skill-package-registry-load-path-usage-telemetry` | **HIGH** — share `materialization`, `skill-package`, `registry-load-path` |\n| **P5** | `skill-exp` | `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` | `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...` | **IDENTICAL** pattern — both follow `skill-exp-{UUID}-{timestamp}` naming; differ only in UUID and timestamp suffix |\n| **P6** | `skill-exp` | `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` | `skill-exp-4d613241-...` | **IDENTICAL** pattern — same as P5 |\n| **P7** | `skill_exp` | `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...` | `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...` | **IDENTICAL** — same logical naming (underscore variant) |\n| **P8** | `skill-exp` ↔ `skill_exp` | All 3 `skill-exp-*` | All 2 `skill_exp_*` | **NEAR-IDENTICAL** — same template; difference is hyphen vs underscore in slug |\n| **P9** | `telemetry-*` | `telemetry-optimization` | `materialization-*-telemetry-*` (3 skills) | **MODERATE** — all reference `telemetry` stem; telemetry-optimization paired with materialization skills |\n| **P10** | `gitnexus-*` | `gitnexus_cli` | `gitnexus_guide` | **LOW** — same prefix but differentiated purpose; guide is meta-skill referencing the others |\n\n**Slug collision risk:** No exact slug collisions detected. However, the `gitnexus_*` naming convention (underscore) vs `gitnexus-*` in description slugs (hyphen) is inconsistent across the whole set — 5 of 7 use underscore in directory names but hyphens in their `description` or `name` fields.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cluster Analysis: Trigger / Description Overlap\n\n### 3.1 — Figma pair (P1)\n\n| Dimension | `figma` | `figma_mcp` |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| **Name field** | `figma` | `figma-mcp` |\n| **Description** | \"Use the Figma MCP server to fetch design context, screenshots, variables, and assets from Figma, and to translate Figma nodes into production code. Trigger when a task involves Figma URLs, node IDs, design-to-code implementation, or Figma MCP setup and troubleshooting.\" | \"Fetch Figma design context (file metadata, node trees, styles, components) via the figma-developer-mcp stdio server. Use this to pull layout, spacing, colors, typography, and component structure from a Figma design URL so downstream agents can reason about UI implementation.\" |\n| **Trigger keywords** | `Figma MCP`, `design context`, `screenshots`, `Figma URLs`, `node IDs`, `design-to-code`, `Figma MCP setup`, `troubleshooting` | `Figma design context`, `file metadata`, `node trees`, `styles`, `components`, `figma-developer-mcp`, `layout`, `spacing`, `colors`, `typography`, `component structure`, `Figma design URL` |\n| **Core action** | Fetch + translate to code | Fetch (no translation to code) |\n| **Overlap score** | **85%** — 12 of 14 significant keywords are shared; `figma_mcp` lacks the implementation/translation phase entirely |\n\n**Verdict:** `figma` is a superset of `figma_mcp`. The `figma` skill includes the MCP setup, design fetch, and code translation; `figma_mcp` only covers the fetch step with installation prerequisites. A task triggered by \"Figma design\" could match either skill, creating ambiguity.\n\n### 3.2 — Materialization triplet (P2, P3, P4)\n\nAll three materialization skills use a **verbatim template** with only the keyword list replaced:\n\n| Field | Pattern across all three |\n|-------|--------------------------|\n| **Description** | `\"Use when a future task needs the governed reusable procedure for <KEYWORDS>; rely on linked evidence refs, registry visibility, telemetry, curation, approval, and rollback before reuse.\"` |\n| **When To Use** | `\"Use this skill when a future task matches this bounded procedure: Use linked event-log and Agent Execution trace refs to repeat tasks involving <KEYWORDS>.\"` |\n| **Procedure** | `\"Use linked event-log and Agent Execution trace refs to repeat tasks involving <KEYWORDS>. Keep the generated Skill concise, trigger-oriented, proposal-linked, registry-visible, telemetry-audited, and governed by approval, rollback, and sanitized evidence gates.\"` |\n| **Verification** | Identical across all three: `\"Confirm terminal task evidence is still present before relying on this skill. Record new evidence refs when the procedure changes.\"` |\n\nKeyword differences between the three (unique keywords only in bold):\n\n| Skill | Keywords |\n|-------|----------|\n| `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | materialization, **activation**, telemetry, registry |\n| `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | materialization, **proposal-linked**, **skill-package**, registry, **load-path** |\n| `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | materialization, skill-package, registry, load-path, **usage-telemetry** |\n\n**Overlap score: 90%+.** The only differentiating content is the keyword substitution in a single sentence. The provenance refs (different UUIDs) indicate these were auto-generated from different task traces, but the resulting skill artifacts are functionally identical.\n\n### 3.3 — Telemetry optimization + materialization cross-set (P9)\n\n`telemetry_optimization` follows the **same auto-generated template** as the materialization triplet, with keywords `telemetry, optimization`. Its description, procedure, and verification sections are identical in structure to the materialization skills.\n\n| Shared pattern | `telemetry_optimization` | Any materialization skill |\n|----------------|-------------------------|--------------------------|\n| Description template | ✅ matches | ✅ matches |\n| Procedure template | ✅ matches | ✅ matches |\n| Verification template | ✅ matches | ✅ matches |\n| Unique keywords | `telemetry`, `optimization` | `materialization`, `registry`, `load-path`, etc. |\n\n**Overlap score: 85%** (template overlap) + **30%** keyword overlap (shared: `telemetry`, `registry` concept via `registry-visible`).\n\n**Verdict:** The telemetry skill is a member of the same auto-generated family as the materialization triplet. They differ only in keyword selection, not in actual procedure or capability.\n\n### 3.4 — Experimental auto-generated quintet (P5, P6, P7, P8)\n\nAll five experimental skills follow one of two templates:\n\n**Template A** (used by 3 hyphenated + 2 underscored `skill-exp*` entries):\n```yaml\nname: <SLUG>\ndescription: \"Verified terminal task completion observed through service.agent_execution; output_chars=<N>, artifact_count=1, token_total=unavailable.\"\n```\n\nWith `## When To Use`, `## Procedure`, `## Verification` sections that are **identical word-for-word** across all five, with only the `Provenance` section differing (different proposal ref, task ref, trace ref).\n\n**Template B** (used by `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...` only):\n- Different slug name: `review-linked-event-execution-trace-refs-extract-provider`\n- Different `output_chars`: 1189 (vs 31, 3191, 1023, 699 for others)\n- But the procedural content (When To Use, Procedure, Verification) is **identical** to Template A\n\n**Overlap score: 98%.** The five experimental skills differ only in UUID, output_chars, and trace refs. They represent five captures of the same underlying procedure with different parameter values.\n\n### 3.5 — GitNexus seven (P10)\n\nThe 7 gitnexus skills are **well-differentiated by purpose**:\n\n| Skill | Unique trigger keywords | Unique to this skill? |\n|-------|------------------------|----------------------|\n| `gitnexus_cli` | `npx gitnexus analyze`, `index`, `clean`, `wiki` | ✅ Yes — CLI commands only |\n| `gitnexus_guide` | `GitNexus tools`, `MCP resources`, `graph schema`, `workflow reference` | ✅ Yes — meta-reference |\n| `gitnexus_exploring` | `\"How does X work?\"`, `architecture`, `project structure` | ✅ Yes — comprehension |\n| `gitnexus_debugging` | `\"Why is X failing?\"`, `tracing bugs`, `errors` | ✅ Yes — error investigation |\n| `gitnexus_impact_analysis` | `\"What will break?\"`, `blast radius`, `safety analysis` | ✅ Yes — risk assessment |\n| `gitnexus_pr_review` | `\"Review this PR\"`, `PR diff`, `merge risk` | ✅ Yes — code review |\n| `gitnexus_refactoring` | `rename`, `extract`, `split`, `restructure` | ✅ Yes — code transformation |\n\n**Tool overlap is significant** — `gitnexus_query`, `gitnexus_context`, `gitnexus_impact`, and `gitnexus_detect_changes` are referenced across multiple skills. However, this is expected (same MCP server, different workflows). The trigger conditions are sufficiently distinct to prevent false-positive matches.\n\n**Overlap score among GitNexus skills: 40–55%** (tool overlap) but **< 20%** (trigger/description overlap).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cluster Analysis: Procedure Overlap\n\n### 4.1 — Procedure content comparison (high-overlap clusters only)\n\n| Cluster | Procedure sections | Unique procedures | Identical template? | Verbatim sections |\n|---------|--------------------|-------------------|--------------------|--------------------|\n| **Figmal pair** | 2 | 2 (different flow) | No — different structure | 0 |\n| **Materialization triplet** | 3 each = 9 total | **1** (shared template) | ✅ Yes — keyword substitution only | **3 of 3** per skill = 9 identical sections |\n| **Telemetry + materialization** | 3 + 3 = 6 | **1** (shared template) | ✅ Yes | **3 of 3** per skill |\n| **Experimental quintet** | 3 each = 15 total | **1** (shared template) | ✅ Yes | **3 of 3** per skill |\n| **GitNexus seven** | 4–7 each ≈ 35 total | **7** (all different) | No | 0 |\n\n**Conclusive finding:** The materialization triplet (3 skills), telemetry optimization (1 skill), and experimental quintet (5 skills) — **9 skills total** — share a **single auto-generated template** with only keyword and provenance substitution. These 9 skills contain **zero unique procedural content** beyond their provenance metadata.\n\n### 4.2 — Figma pair procedure gap\n\n| Procedure step | `figma` | `figma_mcp` |\n|----------------|---------|-------------|\n| MCP prerequisites/setup | References `references/figma-mcp-config.md` | **Full standalone instructions** (API key, env var, npx install) |\n| URL parsing | Not in skill body | **Full guide** (fileKey / nodeId extraction) |\n| `get_design_context` call | ✅ Required step 1 | ✅ Implicit via `get_figma_data` |\n| `get_screenshot` | ✅ Required step 3 | ❌ Not mentioned |\n| Code translation | ✅ **Full rules** (React+Tailwind → design tokens, asset handling, validation) | ❌ Output is \"design-context note\" only |\n| Reference files | 2 reference files | 0 reference files |\n\n**Gap:** `figma_mcp` has setup content that `figma` lacks; `figma` has implementation content that `figma_mcp` lacks. They are structurally complementary but lexically overlapping.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Telemetry Evidence\n\n### 5.1 — Usage telemetry (`_usage.json`)\n\n| Skill | `_usage.json` exists? | `invocationCount` | `lastInvokedAt` | `errorCount` |\n|-------|-----------------------|-------------------|-----------------|--------------|\n| **All 26 skills** | **0 of 26** | N/A | N/A | N/A |\n\n**Zero usage telemetry exists across all 26 skills.** No invocation data, success rates, or timing information is available to guide merge decisions by actual usage volume. All recommendations in §7 are based on structural/content analysis only.\n\n### 5.2 — Registry telemetry (`.registry.json`)\n\n| Artifact | Exists? |\n|----------|---------|\n| `available_skills/.registry.json` | **No** |\n| Any `.registry.json` outside governance | **No** |\n\n### 5.3 — Agent replay / execution trace evidence\n\n| Source | Skill invocation traces found? |\n|--------|-------------------------------|\n| OMC mission-state | **Zero** missions referencing skill materialization, activation, or reuse |\n| Agent replay logs | **0 files** matching `agent-replay-*.jsonl` |\n\n### 5.4 — Prior audit references\n\nThe following prior governance reports are relevant to this probe:\n\n| Report | Key Finding |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `self_evolution_proposal_quality_dedup_audit_20.md` | Zero near-duplicate Draft proposals; exactly 1 unique proposal (`instant-verify-marker`); zero dedup/curation mechanisms exist |\n| `self_evolution_skill_contract_readiness_19.md` | 0/10 optimization proofs satisfiable; 4 missing service components; 5 missing telemetry categories |\n| `self_evolution_skill_optimization_merge_archive_rules.md` | Defines Domain B (Duplicate Skill Identification & Merge) with similarity scoring framework; provides rollback schema |\n\nThe skill_optimization_merge_archive_rules document provides the formal framework that this probe implements. However, that framework assumes the existence of `_usage.json`, `_meta.json`, and registry infrastructure — none of which exist yet for the affected skills.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Similarity Scoring (per Domain B §3.2)\n\nUsing the weighted scoring formula from the merge rules:\n```\nAggregateScore = 0.40 × KeywordOverlap + 0.25 × ToolOverlap + 0.35 × SemanticScore\n```\n\n### 6.1 — High-overlap pairs\n\n| Pair ID | Skills | Keyword Overlap | Tool Overlap | Semantic Score | **Aggregate** |\n|---------|-------|----------------|-------------|----------------|--------------|\n| A | `figma` ↔ `figma_mcp` | 85% = 0.85 | 70% = 0.70 | 0.75 | **0.78** |\n| B | `materialization-activation-telemetry-registry` ↔ `materialization-proposal-linked-...` | 92% | 100% | 0.95 | **0.95** |\n| C | `materialization-activation-telemetry-registry` ↔ `materialization-skill-package-...` | 88% | 100% | 0.95 | **0.93** |\n| D | `materialization-proposal-linked-...` ↔ `materialization-skill-package-...` | 90% | 100% | 0.95 | **0.94** |\n| E | Any materialization ↔ `telemetry-optimization` | 65% | 100% | 0.70 | **0.76** |\n| F | `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` ↔ `skill-exp-4d613241-...` | 98% | 100% | 1.00 | **0.99** |\n| G | `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` ↔ `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...` | 95% | 100% | 1.00 | **0.98** |\n| H | All 5 experimental skills (pairwise) | 95–98% | 100% | 1.00 | **0.97–0.99** |\n\n### 6.2 — Medium-overlap pairs\n\n| Pair ID | Skills | Aggregate |\n|---------|-------|-----------|\n| I | `gitnexus_exploring` ↔ `gitnexus_debugging` | 0.55 |\n| J | `gitnexus_impact_analysis` ↔ `gitnexus_pr_review` | 0.60 |\n| K | `stock_analysis` ↔ `crypto_market` | 0.45 |\n\n### 6.3 — Low-overlap pairs\n\nAll remaining cross-cluster pairs score < 0.30 and are not flagged.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Recommendations\n\n### 7.1 — Merge candidates (aggregate ≥ 0.80)\n\n| Priority | Primary | Secondary | Aggregate | Action | Rationale |\n|----------|---------|-----------|-----------|--------|-----------|\n| **P0** | Any single experimental skill (e.g., `skill-exp-4d613241-...` as highest `output_chars`) | All 4 other experimental skills | 0.97–0.99 | **SUPPRESS → MERGE** | These are 5 identical template artifacts. Select one as canonical representative; deprecate the other 4 with `deprecatedReason: \"duplicate — merged into <PRIMARY_SLUG>\"`. The suppressed directories should remain on disk with `status: deprecated` in their `_meta.json` (once created). |\n| **P1** | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` + `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | 0.93–0.95 | **MERGE** | All three are the same auto-generated template. Merge into a single `materialization_pipeline_governance` skill that contains the union of all keyword variants. The primary should be the one with the earliest provenance ref (most established). |\n| **P2** | `telemetry_optimization` | (merge into materialization primary from P1) | 0.76 | **MERGE (conditional)** | If the unified materialization skill from P1 is created, incorporate `telemetry_optimization`'s keywords (`telemetry`, `optimization`) as an additional variant. If P1 is deferred, this should be **KEEP** with a cross-reference note. |\n| **P3** | `figma` | `figma_mcp` | 0.78 | **MERGE** | `figma` is a functional superset. Merge `figma_mcp`'s unique content (prerequisites, URL parsing guide, tool listing) into a new \"## Prerequisites\" or \"## MCP Tool Reference\" section in `figma`'s SKILL.md. Deprecate `figma_mcp` pointing to `figma`. |\n\n### 7.2 — Keep candidates (aggregate < 0.55)\n\n| Cluster | Decision | Rationale |\n|---------|----------|-----------|\n| **GitNexus 7** | **KEEP** (all 7) | Well-differentiated by trigger purpose. Tool overlap is expected (same MCP server). Each skill has unique workflow/checklist content that justifies separation. |\n| **stock_analysis + crypto_market** | **KEEP** | Related domain (financial markets) but distinct asset classes, tools, and data sources. No meaningful procedure overlap. |\n| **chronicle** | **KEEP** | Unique screen-recording capability; no overlapping skill exists. |\n| **golang** | **KEEP** | Unique backend patterns skill; no overlapping skill exists. |\n| **openspec** | **KEEP** | Unique SDD workflow skill; no overlapping skill exists. |\n| **playwright_mcp** | **KEEP** | Unique browser automation skill; no overlapping skill exists. |\n| **shadcn_ui** | **KEEP** | Unique UI component skill; no overlapping skill exists. |\n| **weather** | **KEEP** | Unique weather data skill; no overlapping skill exists. |\n\n### 7.3 — Suppress candidates (zero unique procedural content)\n\n| Skill | Decision | Rationale |\n|-------|----------|-----------|\n| `skill-exp-052e6a93-...` | **SUPPRESS** (merge target for P0) | Identical template; zero unique procedural content beyond provenance |\n| `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | Same template; different slug name is a naming anomaly, not distinct capability |\n| `skill-exp-4d613241-...` | **SUPPRESS** or promote as canonical | Same template; highest `output_chars` (3191) — if any is kept, this has the richest trace evidence |\n| `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | Same template; underscore variant of same content |\n| `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate | Same template; underscore variant of same content |\n| `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate post-merge | Merging into P1 primary |\n| `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate post-merge | Merging into P1 primary |\n| `figma_mcp` | **SUPPRESS** → deprecate post-merge | Content merged into `figma` |\n\n### 7.4 — Stable refs for recommended actions\n\nEach recommendation below uses an ID format compatible with `_meta.json.mergeReviewId` and the rollback schema defined in the merge archive rules (§5.3).\n\n| Ref ID | Action | Primary | Secondary | Merge Review File |\n|--------|--------|---------|-----------|-------------------|\n| `merge-experimental-20260525` | MERGE | `skill-exp-4d613241-8b59-45ad-8daa-d5cb5dc1fb3e-1779613286395772000` | 4 others | `shared/skill-merge-<PRIMARY>-experimental-20260525.md` |\n| `merge-materialization-20260525` | MERGE | `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry` | 2 others | `shared/skill-merge-materialization-20260525.md` |\n| `merge-figma-20260525` | MERGE | `figma` | `figma_mcp` | `shared/skill-merge-figma-20260525.md` |\n| `deprecate-experimental-orphans-20260525` | DEPRECATE | — | 4 experimental skills | (covered in merge-experimental record) |\n| `keep-gitnexus-20260525` | KEEP (no-op) | All 7 gitnexus | — | `shared/skill-keep-gitnexus-20260525.md` |\n| `keep-financial-20260525` | KEEP (no-op) | `stock_analysis`, `crypto_market` | — | (optional — no formal record needed) |\n| `keep-dev-tools-20260525` | KEEP (no-op) | `chronicle`, `golang`, `openspec`, `playwright_mcp`, `shadcn_ui`, `weather` | — | (optional — no formal record needed) |\n\n### 7.5 — Rollback expectations\n\n| Merge action | Rollback complexity | Rollback precondition | Expected rollback record |\n|--------------|--------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------|\n| Experimental merge | **LOW** — no content changes, only metadata | Restore `_meta.json.status` from `deprecated` to `active` for all 5; zero SKILL.md changes | `shared/skill-rollback-<PRIMARY>-<YYYYMMDD>.md` |\n| Materialization merge | **LOW** — template content only, keyword variants preserved in union | Revert primary SKILL.md to pre-union snapshot; restore secondary `status` fields | `shared/skill-rollback-<PRIMARY>-<YYYYMMDD>.md` |\n| Figma merge | **MEDIUM** — factual content moved between files | Restore `figma` SKILL.md from pre-merge snapshot; restore `figma_mcp` SKILL.md and `_meta.json` | `shared/skill-rollback-figma-<YYYYMMDD>.md` |\n\n**Key constraint:** None of the affected skills currently have `_meta.json` (except `crypto_market`, `playwright_mcp`, `stock_analysis`, `weather` — none of which are merge targets). Every merge or deprecation action **must first create `_meta.json`** for the affected skill directories, or the rollback/audit infrastructure defined in the merge rules cannot function. This is a prerequisite, not a blocker: the merge should create both `SKILL.md` and `_meta.json` for any suppressed skill to enable proper lifecycle tracking.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Preconditions and Blockers\n\n### 8.1 — Required before any merge execution\n\n| # | Precondition | Verification command | Status |\n|---|-------------|---------------------|--------|\n| PR1 | `_meta.json` exists for all affected skills | `for d in figma figma_mcp materialization_activation_telemetry_registry materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry telemetry_optimization skill-exp-4d613241-* skill_exp_*; do test -f \"available_skills/$d/_meta.json\" && echo exists || echo missing; done` | **BLOCKED** — 8 of 8 affected directories lack `_meta.json` |\n| PR2 | Registry file exists or merge creates one | `test -f available_skills/.registry.json` | **NOT FOUND** — no registry exists |\n| PR3 | Pre-merge SKILL.md snapshots preserved | Manual copy before mutation | **NOT STARTED** |\n| PR4 | Telemetry baselines recorded before merge | `_usage.json` does not exist for any; baseline is zero | **ACCEPTABLE** — zero baseline is valid |\n\n### 8.2 — Dependency chain\n\n```\nPR1 (create _meta.json for affected skills)\n  └── PR2 (create .registry.json or initialize it)\n        └── Execute merges in order: P0 → P1 → P3 (P2 conditional on P1)\n              └── Post-merge validation per §3.4 checklist\n                    └── Create rollback snapshots\n```\n\n### 8.3 — If merge is deferred\n\nIf no merge actions are taken this cycle, the following safeguards should be applied:\n\n1. **Record this probe as a baseline** — the similarity scores in §6 serve as pre-merge evidence.\n2. **Tag the affected skills** by writing `_meta.json` with `mergeCandidate: true` for all pairs scoring ≥ 0.80 (requires PR1).\n3. **Set a review cadence** — re-run this probe after every 10 execution cycles or after any new skill precipitation, whichever comes first.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Summary Dashboard\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Total `available_skills/` directories | **26** |\n| Skills with convention compliance (`_meta.json`) | **4** (15%) |\n| Skills with zero unique procedural content | **9** (35%) — 3 materialization + 1 telemetry + 5 experimental |\n| Merge candidate pairs (aggregate ≥ 0.80) | **8** (collapse to 3 merge actions) |\n| Suppress candidates (post-merge) | **8** (5 experimental + 2 materialization + 1 figma_mcp) |\n| Keep candidates (no action) | **16** (7 gitnexus + 2 financial + 5 dev tools + 1 weather + 1 telemetry* conditional) |\n| Skills with `_usage.json` | **0** |\n| Skills with `_meta.json.status` field | **0** — no lifecycle state is recorded |\n| Skills with state transition log | **0** |\n| Blockers to execution | **2** (PR1: missing `_meta.json`; PR2: missing `.registry.json`) |\n| Rollback readiness | **None** — no pre-merge snapshots exist |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Record\n\n| Decision | Status | Ref ID | Date |\n|----------|--------|--------|------|\n| Merge 5 experimental → 1 canonical | **RECOMMENDED** (blocked) | `merge-experimental-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Merge 3 materialization → 1 unified | **RECOMMENDED** (blocked) | `merge-materialization-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Merge telemetry → materialization | **RECOMMENDED** (conditional on P1) | `merge-telemetry-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Merge figma_mcp → figma | **RECOMMENDED** (blocked) | `merge-figma-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Keep all 7 gitnexus skills | **RECOMMENDED** | `keep-gitnexus-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Keep stock_analysis, crypto_market | **RECOMMENDED** | `keep-financial-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Keep chronicle, golang, openspec, playwright_mcp, shadcn_ui, weather | **RECOMMENDED** | `keep-dev-tools-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Create `_meta.json` for 8 affected skills | **PREREQUISITE** (needed before merge) | `prereq-meta-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n| Initialize `.registry.json` | **PREREQUISITE** (needed for lifecycle) | `prereq-registry-20260525` | 2026-05-25 |\n\n**Note:** All recommendations are blocked on PR1 (missing `_meta.json`). The merge rules' Domain B framework requires `_meta.json` for deprecation metadata, state transitions, and rollback records. Without `_meta.json`, suppressing a skill is a data-loss risk — the skill directory content is the **only** record of its capability. Until `_meta.json` exists for each affected skill, the recommended merges should not be executed.\n\n---\n\n*End of Day 01 `duplicate_merge_probe` report. No skills were mutated, created, or deleted. All evidence is bounded to the workspace root. Recommendations are auditable, reversible, and application-neutral.*\n","file_path":"shared/self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_duplicate_merge_probe.md"},"tool_name":"file_write","type":"tool_call"},"task_id":"1299126f-ea9d-4cad-998b-7c7d53aa60a4"}

