data: {"agent":"coordinator","agent_tab":"coordinator","output":"Created `shared/self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_duplicate_merge_probe.md` (373 lines). Here's the executive summary:\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 9 skills are auto-generated template clones\n- **3 materialization_* skills** + **1 telemetry_optimization** + **5 skill-exp* experimental skills** = **9 skills with zero unique procedural content**. Their SKILL.md files are identical except for keyword substitution and provenance UUIDs. Aggregate similarity scores: **0.93–0.99**.\n\n### 2 Figma skills overlap at 85%+\n- `figma` is a functional superset of `figma_mcp`. The latter has setup instructions the former lacks, but the former has code-translation rules the latter lacks. **Merge recommended** (score: 0.78).\n\n### 7 GitNexus skills — keep all\n- Well-differentiated by purpose (CLI vs debugging vs exploring vs impact analysis vs PR review vs refactoring vs guide). Tool overlap is expected (same MCP server). **No merge needed.**\n\n### 2 blockers prevent execution\n| Blocker | Issue |\n|---------|-------|\n| **PR1** | 8 of 8 affected skills lack `_meta.json` — no lifecycle state, no merge metadata, no rollback infrastructure |\n| **PR2** | No `.registry.json` exists — no discovery mechanism for post-merge registration |\n\n### Merge plan (3 actions)\n1. **P0** — 5 experimental → 1 canonical (score 0.99)\n2. **P1** — 3 materialization + 1 telemetry → 1 unified (score 0.93–0.95)\n3. **P3** — figma_mcp → figma (score 0.78)\n\nAll recommendations include stable refs (`merge-experimental-20260525`, etc.), rollback expectations, and pre/post validation checklists — per the Domain B framework defined in `self_evolution_skill_optimization_merge_archive_rules.md`.","success":true,"task_id":"1299126f-ea9d-4cad-998b-7c7d53aa60a4"}

